    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today with a high-floor offensive outlook, anchored by elite matchups against weak opposing arms. **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber** headline our top-tier plays, both benefiting from an aggressive +19% boost due to a soft matchup against Sasaki (5.11 xERA). **Trea Turner** leads the team in efficiency with a 76.35 score, providing the ideal combination of order priority and pitchability. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a cornerstone of the lineup; despite facing a neutral arm in Sproat, his elite 0.424 xwOBA ensures he maintains a stellar 73.62 score. **Kazuma Okamoto** is also a standout today; his 69.87 projection is buoyed significantly by a +16% park factor adjustment, making him a high-leverage start at 3B.\n\nThe decision-making process for the utility spot was razor-thin, as **Junior Caminero** ultimately earned the start despite a difficult matchup against Detmers (3.10 xERA). His score of 45.87 barely surpassed the threshold, narrowly edging out **Caleb Durbin**, whose projection of 39.98 fell just short of our 40-point \"Below Floor\" policy. **Caleb Durbin** was dinged primarily by a challenging SP skill rating and a suboptimal bottom-of-the-order placement, which outweighed his base skill profile. Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the 33% rain risk surrounding **Pete Crow-Armstrong** in his leadoff role; while his 71.82 score is enticing, we must remain prepared to pivot if the game in his venue is delayed or postponed. Outside of that weather risk, we are capitalizing on the favorable SP profiles today to maximize our chances across all five roto categories.",
